<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        com.mitchell.stack-ops.stray-drain

        Drains unwrapped Claude Code transcripts into vault session records at
        01:30 and 13:30 PT, half an hour ahead of nightly-hygiene.

        WHY IT IS SCHEDULED. /wrap mines at most 8 strays per run, because it
        reads each transcript into the INTERACTIVE session's context. That cap is
        a context budget, not a correctness bound, so the backlog outran it: on
        2026-08-07 there were 871 unwrapped transcripts against a 3,190-entry
        ledger. What then happens is a live session finding hundreds of strays,
        correctly judging that mining them is too much context-heavy work for an
        already-drifting model, and declining. Reporting a stray count is not
        capturing the information. Draining is mechanical and bounded, so it
        belongs on a schedule and not in anyone's context window.

        ROUTING. Summarisation goes to the cheap open-weight tier via `cheap
        --task bulk_summarize`, measured at about $0.004 per transcript. The
        privacy gate refuses transcripts referencing .env, .secrets, .zshrc or a
        credential vault; those are re-run with --engine claude, which routes
        through ~/.claude/bin/claude so they bill the SUBSCRIPTION and the
        content never reaches a third party. Never make claude the general
        engine here: that is a metered-billing path for bulk toil.

        SAFETY. Never deletes a transcript. Claims each through the locked wrap
        ledger so concurrent /wrap runs cannot double-mine. Commits only new
        session records by explicit path, never `git add -A`, because 10 to 30
        concurrent sessions write this vault.

        node is the entrypoint because TCC grants are per binary: /bin/zsh under
        launchd is denied ~/Documents, node at its absolute path is granted, and
        children inherit the grant. Log paths live OUTSIDE ~/Documents per the
        2026-05-21 sandbox finding.

        Bootstrap:
          mkdir -p ~/Library/Logs/stack-ops/stray-drain
          cp scripts/launchd/com.mitchell.stack-ops.stray-drain.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
          launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mitchell.stack-ops.stray-drain.plist

        Run by hand:
          node ~/Documents/stack-ops/scripts/memory-sweep/stray-drain.mjs --dry-run
    -->

    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.mitchell.stack-ops.stray-drain</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/mitchellwilliams/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/node</string>
        <string>/Users/mitchellwilliams/Documents/stack-ops/scripts/memory-sweep/stray-drain.mjs</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/mitchellwilliams</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key>
            <integer>1</integer>
            <key>Minute</key>
            <integer>30</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key>
            <integer>13</integer>
            <key>Minute</key>
            <integer>30</integer>
        </dict>
    </array>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/mitchellwilliams/Library/Logs/stack-ops/stray-drain/launchd.out</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/mitchellwilliams/Library/Logs/stack-ops/stray-drain/launchd.err</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/Users/mitchellwilliams/.claude/bin:/Users/mitchellwilliams/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/mitchellwilliams</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
